The Rustium License

Copyright (c) 2026 Christian Jay (Christianzz4603) and Rustium contributors

Hi! Rustium is free for you to use. Build on it, change it, ship it, even sell
what you make with it. I only ask that you follow the few simple rules below.

This license is based on the well-known MIT license, with a couple of extra
terms I care about (rules 2 and 3).

THE RULES

1. Keep my name on it.
   Keep this license and the copyright line above in every copy of Rustium, or
   of any big piece of it, that you share. If you ship a product, website, or
   app built on Rustium, please give credit somewhere people can actually find
   it, like an About page, a credits screen, or your README. Something like
   "Built on Rustium by Christian Jay (Christianzz4603)" is perfect.
   If you change Rustium, say so, and don't make it look like I approve of or
   built your version.

2. What you make is yours, and so is the responsibility.
   I'm happy to see what people build, but I can't control it, and I'm not
   responsible for it. If something you create with Rustium is dangerous,
   illegal, or hurts someone, that's on you, not on me or the other people who
   worked on Rustium. Please follow the laws that apply to you (privacy,
   security, copyright, export rules, and so on), and don't use Rustium to
   break the law or to hurt people or their systems. And please don't say or
   imply that I'm okay with that kind of use.

3. Don't use my name to sell yours.
   You can use the credit from rule 1, but please don't use the names "Rustium"
   or "Christian Jay" / "Christianzz4603" to promote your own product without
   asking me first.

4. If you break the rules, the permission stops.
   Your permission to use Rustium ends automatically if you break these terms.
   Stop breaking them and it comes back.

